comment.narrative:
1.Innovative activity refers to new to firm number of products or processes introduced following the Frascati manual definition; gender of each head of the organization will be recorded.

- 108 innovative activities were completed by 27 sub-projects incude:&nbsp;

+ Products recognized by National Office of Intellectual Property - MOST: 46 patents/Utility solutions; 10 trade marks; 05 products with registered industrial designs

&nbsp;+ Products recognized by United States Patent and Trademark Offce (USPT O): 02 patents

+ Products recognized by Copyright Office of Vietnam, Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism: 20 copyrights;

+ Products recognized by Department of Crop Production, Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development - MARD: 17 copyrights;

+ Products recognized by Directorate of Fisheries, Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development - MARD: 05 copyrights;

+ 9 out of 27 sub-projects with female leader(s) in SPMU management???????

1. This indicator is newly added from April 2018&nbsp;to capture the &quot;effectiveness&quot; aspect of the PDO.

2. Definition: Consortia sub-project is considered completed when the innovative product(s) or solution(s) under the sub-project is deemed to be commercialization-ready, new technology processes and new production processes are successfully completed and transferred.&nbp;

3.&nbsp;The achievement of 14 against EOP target of 15 is because several consortia dropped out after signing the grant agreement for various reasons, including changes in enterprise priority focus, funding secured through alternative resources, and unforeseen financial difficulties faced by the enterprise.
